job_description:
This is Adyen

Adyen provides payments, data, and financial products in a single solution for customers like Meta, Uber, H&amp;M, and Microsoft - making us the financial technology platform of choice. At Adyen, everything we do is engineered for ambition.&nbsp;

For our teams, we create an environment with opportunities for our people to succeed, backed by the culture and support to ensure they are enabled to truly own their careers. We are motivated individuals who tackle unique technical challenges at scale and solve them as a team. Together, we deliver innovative and ethical solutions that help businesses achieve their ambitions faster.

Team Lead, Scaled Account Management London

Our Scaled Account Management team in London provides the best experience to our portfolio of mid-sized, fast-growth merchants. We achieve this using a pooled Account Management approach focusing on efficiency and proactivity, regularly reaching out to our merchants to identify additional service opportunities, such as international payment methods, fraud management services, or point-of-sale opportunities. With a strategic mindset and hands-on approach, this team drives growth and retention in our UK portfolio as we scale.

&nbsp;

Here are some examples of your team's responsibilities:

• Build strong relationships with your merchants

• Drive commercial growth

• Accelerate product adoption

• Consult and train key stakeholders&nbsp;

• Manage time-sensitive, cross-functional initiatives and projects in a fast-paced, highly entrepreneurial environment&nbsp;

What you'll do:

As the Team Lead, your role and some of your responsibilities will include:

• Team management: you are lucky to start with a great team and they deserve a leader; committed to help them grow and give their best. You will coach, support, manage workload and keep the work fair and fun; Create and maintain an inspiring and collaborative team environment with an open communication/feedback culture;

• Commercial target ownership and delivery: targets are annual and are achieved at a team level. Ensuring every team member is contributing at an individual level.&nbsp;

• Drive scalability initiatives and projects: together with other global AM Leads to strengthen our efforts towards automation, smarter usage of commercial tools&nbsp; and "Account Management at scale” to achieve higher productivity and increased customer satisfaction;

• Lead the day to day: when needed, get involved in operational tasks and support the team in merchant escalation calls or critical negotiations;

• Hire, develop and retain diverse talents: the team needs to keep growing to support our commercial and strategic ambitions;

• Align and collaborate with internal teams: primarily Marketing, Sales, Partnership, Account Management and operations to provide outstanding Customer Experience to merchants;&nbsp;

Who you are

• 5+ years of experience in a customer-facing B2B role, preferably Account Management/Customer Success/Sales;&nbsp;

• 3+ years of experience managing a team;&nbsp;

• You have owned commercial targets: you have a proven commercial edge and strong negotiation skills, good judgment and consultative acumen;&nbsp;

• You have good leadership and interpersonal skills: you listen, you have empathy, you can communicate effectively and convince when necessary;

• You like thinking big picture and scale and you want to be part of further shaping our AM Service level proposition;

• You have a genuine interest and technical aptitude / understanding of our products &amp; industry;

• You know what DEI means and you have ideas on how to take it into account in your decision making process continuously;

• You have experience in leading hiring processes and can identify talents;

Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion at Adyen

We actively seek different perspectives to sharpen our ideas. Our unique culture is a product of our diverse backgrounds and experiences. No matter who you are or where you’re from, you’re welcome to be your true self at Adyen.&nbsp;

If you need accommodations or support during the recruitment process to perform at your best, you’ll have the opportunity to let our team know in your application. We encourage people from all backgrounds and abilities to apply.

What’s next?

Ensuring a smooth and enjoyable candidate experience is critical for us. We aim to get back to you regarding your application within 5 business days. Our interview process tends to take about 4 weeks to complete, but may fluctuate depending on the role. Learn more about our hiring process here. Don’t be afraid to let us know if you need more flexibility.

&nbsp;

This role is based out of our London office. We are an office-first company and value in-person collaboration; we do not offer remote-only roles.

Why Choose Bottomline?

Are you ready to transform the way businesses pay and get paid? Bottomline is a global leader in business payments and cash management, with over 35 years of experience and moving more than $16 trillion in payments annually. We're looking for passionate individuals to join our team and help drive impactful results for our customers. If you're dedicated to delighting customers and promoting growth and innovation - we want you on our team!

Position Title&nbsp;

Order &amp; Billing Associate&nbsp;

Department&nbsp;

Finance Operations / Order &amp; Billing Operations&nbsp;

Reports To&nbsp;

Order &amp; Billing Team Lead / Manager, Order &amp; Billing Operations&nbsp;

Location&nbsp;

United Kingdom (Hybrid)&nbsp;

&nbsp;Please note this is an Entry level role.

Position Summary&nbsp;

Bottomline is seeking an Order &amp; Billing Associate to join the Global Order &amp; Billing Operations team. This role is responsible for supporting the end-to-end processing of customer orders, billing activities, customer account maintenance, and operational administration for a portfolio of strategic UK banking customers.&nbsp;

The position focuses on the accurate and timely processing of customer onboarding requests, sales orders, billing transactions, invoice distribution, customer account updates, and month-end billing activities. The successful candidate will work closely with internal teams, banking customers, and third-party suppliers to ensure service levels are achieved while maintaining a high degree of accuracy and compliance with established procedures.&nbsp;

This role requires strong attention to detail, the ability to follow documented processes, effective time management, and excellent customer service skills.&nbsp;

&nbsp;

Essential Duties and Responsibilities&nbsp;

Order Management&nbsp;

• Process daily onboarding requests for strategic customers utilizing enriched onboarding files.&nbsp;

• Process sales orders for strategic customers using both standard order submissions and enriched files.&nbsp;

• Process sales orders for strategic customers in accordance with documented procedures.&nbsp;

• Complete order amendments, customer change requests, cancellations, and billing-related updates.&nbsp;

• Maintain customer master data including purchase orders, billing addresses, and account details.&nbsp;

• Ensure all required approvals and supporting documentation are obtained prior to processing.&nbsp;

White Label Banking Operations&nbsp;

Support operational activities for strategic banking customers.&nbsp;&nbsp;

Provide support for strategic customers, including management of complex product and project billing requirements that may fall outside standard operational processes.&nbsp;

Billing Operations&nbsp;

• Execute monthly billing activities for assigned accounts.&nbsp;

• Complete month-end B2K file preparation and submission within required service deadlines.&nbsp;

• Perform month-end BITE billing activities on Day 1 of the monthly close cycle using BITE reporting data.&nbsp;

• Process manual billing transactions in accordance with approved procedures.&nbsp;

• Support billing exception management, invoice corrections, credit requests, and rebills.&nbsp;

• Process credits, cancellations, and customer billing adjustments as required.&nbsp;

• Support BTS billing activities until a long-term process is implemented.&nbsp;

• Provide backup support for Professional Services invoicing activities.&nbsp;

Customer Administration&nbsp;

• Update customer purchase orders and associated account information.&nbsp;

• Maintain customer billing and contact records.&nbsp;

• Support customer account maintenance activities to ensure billing accuracy.&nbsp;

MFA Token Management&nbsp;

• Manage daily MFA token dispatch activities.&nbsp;

• Coordinate with external suppliers to arrange customer token shipments.&nbsp;

• Prepare and submit required dispatch reports by established daily deadlines.&nbsp;

• Process and manage MFA token returns received at the office.&nbsp;

• Maintain tracking records and supporting documentation.&nbsp;

Invoice Distribution and Controls&nbsp;

• Retrieve printed invoices from the office and coordinate distribution to customers.&nbsp;

• Perform invoice delivery checks to ensure successful customer receipt.&nbsp;

• Support global invoice reconciliation activities to ensure billing completeness.&nbsp;

• Assist with identifying and resolving invoice delivery exceptions.&nbsp;

Month-End Support&nbsp;

• Support critical month-end processing activities.&nbsp;

• Meet established cutoff times and customer-specific delivery requirements.&nbsp;

• Assist with reconciliations and billing validation processes.&nbsp;

• Escalate issues that may impact monthly close timelines.&nbsp;

&nbsp;

Required Skills and Qualifications&nbsp;

• Strong attention to detail and commitment to data accuracy.&nbsp;

• Ability to manage multiple priorities and deadlines simultaneously.&nbsp;

• Excellent written and verbal communication skills.&nbsp;

• Strong customer service orientation.&nbsp;

• Proficiency with Microsoft Excel, Outlook, and Word.&nbsp;

• Ability to follow documented processes and procedures consistently.&nbsp;

• Ability to work effectively both independently and within a team environment.&nbsp;

&nbsp;Nice to have but not essential:

• Previous experience in order processing, billing administration, customer service, finance operations, or a related administrative role.&nbsp;

&nbsp;

Preferred Qualifications&nbsp;

• Experience supporting order-to-cash, billing, or invoicing processes.&nbsp;

• Experience working with banking or financial services customers.&nbsp;

• Experience using ERP and CRM systems such as D365 and Salesforce.&nbsp;

• Experience performing reconciliations and operational controls.&nbsp;

&nbsp;

Core Competencies&nbsp;

Attention to Detail&nbsp;

Maintains high levels of accuracy when processing orders, invoices, customer records, and billing transactions.&nbsp;

Customer Focus&nbsp;

Delivers responsive and professional support to internal and external customers.&nbsp;

Organization &amp; Time Management&nbsp;

Effectively prioritizes work to meet daily operational deadlines and month-end commitments.&nbsp;

Teamwork&nbsp;

Collaborates effectively with colleagues, suppliers, and business stakeholders.&nbsp;

Accountability&nbsp;

Takes ownership of assigned tasks and follows issues through to completion.&nbsp;

Continuous Improvement&nbsp;

Identifies opportunities to improve efficiency, reduce manual effort, and enhance process consistency.&nbsp;

&nbsp;

Work Environment&nbsp;

• Hybrid UK-based role.&nbsp;

• Standard office and remote working environment.&nbsp;

• Ability to support daily operational cutoffs and month-end processing deadlines.&nbsp;

• Occasional attendance at the office may be required to support invoice distribution and MFA token return activities.&nbsp;

&nbsp;
We welcome talent at all career stages and are dedicated to understanding and supporting additional needs. We're proud to be an equal opportunity employer, committed to creating an inclusive and open environment for everyone.

Why Choose Bottomline?

Are you ready to transform the way businesses pay and get paid? Bottomline is a global leader in business payments and cash management, with over 35 years of experience and moving more than $16 trillion in payments annually. We're looking for passionate individuals to join our team and help drive impactful results for our customers. If you're dedicated to delighting customers and promoting growth and innovation - we want you on our team!

Senior Product Manager&nbsp;

Accounts Payable Automation&nbsp;

A critical product delivery role responsible for advancing Bottomline's strategic AP Automation roadmap and using AI to increase the speed, quality and impact of Product Management work.&nbsp;

Who Are We?&nbsp;

Bottomline is on a mission to be the world's leading business payments company, transforming the way businesses pay and get paid. We serve financial institutions and companies around the world, with teams across North America and EMEA collaborating to deliver innovative financial technology solutions.&nbsp;

Culture and Values&nbsp;

We are one global team, working with and for each other to delight customers through excellent execution and create sustained business value for our customers, our team and our partners. Our culture encourages people to be brave and curious, drive to closure and live our principles every day.&nbsp;

Role&nbsp;

We are looking for an experienced Senior Product Manager to play a critical role in the continued development and delivery of Bottomline's Accounts Payable Automation solutions.&nbsp;

This position is responsible for the product management and delivery of several critical capabilities within AP Automation related to data capture, data quality and validation, and machine learning for automated coding. These capabilities sit at the front end of the invoice automation process and are fundamental to helping customers reduce manual work, improve processing quality and move toward increasingly intelligent, straight-through invoice processing.&nbsp;

The Senior Product Manager translates product strategy and priorities into clearly defined requirements and works closely with Engineering, Architecture, Operations, UX/design, data science and Product leadership to turn those requirements into high-quality capabilities.&nbsp;

This individual must be a proven, AI-forward product leader. AI should not be viewed solely as functionality built into our products. It should also fundamentally change how Product Management work gets done. The Senior Product Manager will actively incorporate AI into day-to-day workflows to increase speed, improve the quality and depth of analysis, accelerate documentation and create more capacity for higher-value product thinking and customer problem solving.&nbsp;

The role is highly collaborative and hands-on. Success requires the ability to move comfortably between product direction and detailed execution, including researching a problem, defining requirements, building structured product requirements documents (PRDs), leading refinement, evaluating design alternatives, reviewing functionality as it is developed, resolving questions during development and validating that delivered capabilities achieve the intended customer and business outcomes.&nbsp;

How You'll Contribute&nbsp;

• Own the execution and delivery of assigned areas of the AP Automation roadmap.&nbsp;

• Translate established product strategy and roadmap priorities into executable product plans, detailed requirements, user stories, acceptance criteria and development-ready documentation.&nbsp;

• Drive assigned initiatives from initial problem definition through design, development, validation, release and ongoing iteration.&nbsp;

• Maintain a clear, prioritized backlog reflecting strategic priorities, customer needs, operational requirements, technical dependencies and delivery commitments.&nbsp;

• Proactively identify requirements gaps, dependencies, risks and decisions that could affect roadmap delivery and drive them to resolution.&nbsp;

• Balance strategic roadmap commitments with customer needs, production considerations, product maintenance and other priorities affecting assigned product areas.&nbsp;

• Maintain urgency and ownership around roadmap execution while ensuring speed does not compromise product quality or customer experience.&nbsp;

• Develop deep expertise in the capabilities for which they are responsible and understand how each contributes to the broader AP Automation experience.&nbsp;

• Incorporate AI into the daily Product Management workflow rather than treating it as an occasional productivity tool. Use AI extensively in the creation and refinement of product documentation while maintaining human ownership and accountability for the resulting requirements.&nbsp;

• Experiment with emerging AI capabilities and workflows, measure whether they materially improve effectiveness and share successful practices with the broader Product organization.&nbsp;

&nbsp;

What We're Looking For&nbsp;

• 

• 2+ years of Product Management, Product Owner or comparable software product experience, preferably within an Agile/SaaS environment.&nbsp;

• Demonstrated experience owning requirements and delivery for complex software products or capabilities.&nbsp;

• Hands on experience using generative AI and AI-enabled tools as part of daily Product Management work.&nbsp;

• Strong ability to translate business and customer needs into detailed PRDs, requirements, user stories, workflows, business rules and acceptance criteria.&nbsp;

• Experience working directly with software Engineering teams throughout the development lifecycle.&nbsp;

• Demonstrated ability to lead effective refinement sessions and ensure requirements are development-ready.&nbsp;

• Strong attention to detail and the ability to evaluate developing functionality against business requirements and intended customer outcomes.&nbsp;

• Ability to understand complex technical and business concepts and communicate effectively across technical and non-technical audiences.&nbsp;

• Strong decision-making skills and the ability to evaluate trade-offs and maintain delivery momentum in a fast-paced environment.&nbsp;

• Excellent written, verbal, presentation and stakeholder-management skills.&nbsp;

• Strong organizational skills with the ability to manage concurrent roadmap priorities, dependencies and deliverables.&nbsp;

• A self-starter who demonstrates ownership, proactively solves problems and drives issues to closure.&nbsp;

• Experience with Accounts Payable, invoice automation, financial technology, document/data capture, machine learning and/or predictive technologies, is highly desirable.&nbsp;

&nbsp;
We welcome talent at all career stages and are dedicated to understanding and supporting additional needs. We're proud to be an equal opportunity employer, committed to creating an inclusive and open environment for everyone.

