 Location
 Hybrid with travel to Reading
 Vacancy Type
 Permanent/Full Time
 Job Summary
 CRM Lead (HubSpot)

You keep HubSpot fit to run Ciphr’s target account model and make it the one place everyone trusts for the numbers. You’ll own the set-up, data quality, routing, scoring and lifecycle stages that demand generation and sales rely on every day, and you’ll fix the issues that stop us knowing what really drives pipeline. Good data is the difference between knowing and guessing, and you’ll be the person who makes sure we know.

Where: Our Reading, Berkshire HQ. You’ll be in the office 2-3 days a week, with the rest from home.

What you’ll do

 • Own HubSpot set-up and governance for demand generation: properties, objects, permissions, workflows and integrations.

 • Design and maintain lifecycle stages, lead and account scoring, and routing, so hot accounts and inbound enquiries reach the right BDR within the agreed SLA.

 • Fix duplicate leads and deals at source, and make lead source, loss reasons and the Target Account field complete and meaningful.

 • Maintain target account tiers, owners and contacts, loading tier moves and enriched accounts from the GTM engineer and data scientist.

 • Run weekly data quality checks and chase owners to close the gaps.

 • Build the dashboards behind the weekly waterfall review: Target, Engaged, Meeting, Opportunity, Won.

 • Support pipeline forecasting with RevOps and the commercial analyst, including stage definitions and probabilities.

 • Build and QA campaign emails, lists, workflows and sequences for programmes and sector sprints.

 • Sync LinkedIn matched audiences with the Tier 1 and Tier 2 account lists.

 • Train and support HubSpot users across marketing, BD and sales, and keep the guidance up to date.

 • Keep CRM data compliant with UK GDPR, consent and retention rules.

What you’ll bring

 • Solid experience as a HubSpot administrator or CRM lead, ideally in B2B SaaS.

 • A strong understanding of CRM data models, lifecycle stages, lead and account scoring, and routing.

 • Experience improving data quality and deduplication at scale.

 • Experience building reports and dashboards that leaders use to make decisions.

 • Experience integrating enrichment and advertising tools such as Clay and LinkedIn.

 • Comfort using AI to speed up data cleansing, documentation and analysis.

 • Attention to detail and a structured approach to change control.

 • Confidence working with RevOps, sales and marketing, and saying no with a reason.

 • HubSpot certifications are an advantage.

What’s in it for you

 • Time for you: 30 days’ annual leave plus bank holidays and your birthday day off.

 • Family matters: Enhanced maternity, adoption, shared parental and paternity pay, plus family-forming time off

 • Money and wellbeing: Pension, life assurance, health cash plan, medical and dental cover after 6 months, and Mental Health First Aiders

 • Growth: Support from our Talent Success Lead to choose the qualifications and development that suit your career goals

 • Plus shopping discounts, cycle to work, Family National Trust membership and a £1,500 employee referral scheme

Who we are

Ciphr is a leading UK provider of HR, payroll, learning and recruitment solutions. Our Payroll Bureau delivers accurate, timely payroll across the UK, from hosted software to fully managed services. We’re a living wage employer, and everyone’s welcome here. Bring your whole self to work, whether you’re creative, outgoing, quiet, courageous or observant.

Ready to join us? Apply today

### Why Collctiv?

##### This is a genuinely big deal.

Collctiv is a FinTech with a mission: make life easier for the people who organise everything for everyone else. We have 2.5 million customers who have used Collctiv to collect over £150M so they can come together and do the things they love with the people they love over 6.8M times. We know where we are going, and this hire is one of the most important steps in getting there.

##### Big visibility. Big responsibility.

There is nowhere to hide at Collctiv, and that is the point. Your decisions shape the company in ways that are simply not possible inside a 500-person business. You work directly alongside our CEO and CTO, with real ownership from day one: not a supporting role, a doing role.

##### Be genuinely part of it

Everyone at Collctiv receives equity options, regardless of role, because every role contributes to what we are building. Work when you work best. Take the holidays you need. We provide everything you need to do the job from home.

##### A path that grows with you

We are rapidly scaling. This role grows in scope, seniority, and reward as you grow into it. We want someone who intends to step up to COO, and we will invest in making that happen.

### The Role

Amy, our CEO, needs to focus on the things only she can do: commercial partnerships, product vision and business strategy. Everything else needs a home. This role is that home.

As Director of Operations, you own the governance, compliance, people, and financial infrastructure of the business. Not as a coordinator or a reviewer: as the person accountable for it. You make decisions. You fix things before anyone notices they need fixing. You build processes that outlast you and documentation that means Collctiv does not depend on any one person.

This role is designed to grow into COO. If you have the instincts of a strong operator but not yet the title, this is your moment.

### Key Responsibilities

##### Compliance & Governance

- Run the day-to-day AML and financial crime compliance programme, owning the processes, decisions, and escalations that sit beneath MLRO level. Our frameworks are already strong: industry-beating dispute, complaint, and SAR rates, backed by proprietary fraud detection software. You are running a well-built machine, not fixing one;
- Act as our named internal Data Protection Officer. You handle DSAR responses, data incidents, and data governance independently. An external DPO supports you on specialist questions; you are the internal point of accountability;
- Own policy review and sign-off, working with our Compliance Manager and Operations Manager so policies no longer reach Amy;
- Handle legal drafting, contract review and regulatory correspondence, escalating to external legal only when genuinely necessary;
- Play a central role - alongside external advisors - on owning and evolving our regulatory position;
- Own the day-to-day relationship with our regulated payment partners and act as the first point of contact for regulatory correspondence.

##### People & Internal Operations

- Own the people infrastructure: progression frameworks, performance reviews, and the 1:1 cadence for non-exec team members. Amy is in the loop only when a decision genuinely needs her;
- Hold the operational rhythm of the business: team cadence, cross-functional accountability, and the ambient awareness that means things get done without chasing;
- Build and maintain internal documentation and operational playbooks so the business does not depend on institutional memory sitting in one person's head;
- Be a line manager people want to work for: one who supports, stretches, and develops the team.

##### Finance & Commercial

- Own month end and financial reporting, working with our external accountants to produce accurate management information without Amy in the loop;
- Support budgeting, forecasting, and board reporting, taking more ownership as your context grows;
- Act as Amy's operational counterpart on commercial partnerships, helping structure, document, and execute the deals she leads;
- Help prepare Collctiv any external review: clean governance, clear metrics, documented processes, a strong narrative.

##### Product & Customer

- Represent the Organiser, our customer, in operational and governance decisions: keep the person who plans everything for everyone else at the centre of how we run the business, not just how we build the product;
- Work with Pete (CTO) where operational and product decisions intersect, able to hold a useful conversation about roadmap priorities and contribute where it counts.

### Type of Person

- You notice things that need doing and do them: without being asked, without waiting for a brief, without needing it in your job title;
- You come from fintech, payments, or a regulated financial services background. You understand that compliance is a competitive advantage when you do it right;
- You are, have been, or could become our customer: an Organiser. The person who books the holiday, chases the money, buys the present. You feel the problem we solve;
- You are comfortable with legal and regulatory language. You can read a contract, draft a policy, and respond to a regulator without hand-holding;
- You communicate with clarity and warmth: open, honest, no ego, willing to get your hands dirty;
- Ambiguity and pace energise you. A small team moving fast is exciting, not daunting;
- You want to grow into this role and beyond it, and you want to be properly rewarded along the way.

### Skills - Essential

We keep this list short deliberately. We want the right person, not a keyword match. That said, four things are non-negotiable:

- Prior experience in a regulated payments or fintech environment, FCA-regulated preferred;
- Working knowledge of AML and financial crime compliance: enough to own day-to-day operations and make sound decisions on escalations;
- Confidence with legal and contractual documents: able to draft, review, and progress without constant external support;
- Real ownership experience inside a startup or scale-up, not just responsibility.

##### Skills - Desirable

- CIMA, ACCA, or equivalent financial qualification (or working toward one);
- Experience as a named DPO or in a data governance role, comfortable handling DSARs and data incidents independently;
- Familiarity with FCA authorisation processes: you do not need to have led one, but you need to understand the landscape;
- Experience building internal documentation, playbooks, or operational wikis;
- Product management exposure: able to write a PRD and contribute meaningfully to roadmap conversations;
- B2B commercial experience: partnerships, contracts, new revenue lines.

### Location & Hours

Collctiv is predominantly remote, with regular time in our Manchester office at a frequency we agree together. Work when you work best. We provide everything you need to do the job from home, and an unlimited holiday policy so you can be all the other versions of yourself that you need to be.

Because this role will be supporting Amy as her right-hand person, being able to come into the office 2-3 days a week would be preferable.

### Salary

£85,000 to £116,000 plus meaningful equity options, monthly wellbeing budget and unlimited holidays. We are transparent about numbers early: we do not waste anyone's time. The package grows as the role grows.

### Apply Because You Absolutely Want To…

- Own real operations at a FinTech with genuine traction and a clear path to exit;
- Take compliance, governance, and people infrastructure entirely off a founder's plate and make it yours;
- Work directly with a founding team who invest in your development, not just your output;
- Build the operational foundations of a business that is going somewhere, and be recognised for it;
- Grow into a COO role, with support, in a business scaling toward an exit;
- Make a real difference to the people who organise everything for everyone else.

### How to Apply

Send an anonymised CV to adam@collctiv.com (we remove unconscious bias from the process from the start). Include brief answers to these two questions:

1. Tell us about something you fixed or built that nobody asked you to. What did you notice, what did you do, and what happened?
2. Why Collctiv, and why this role specifically?

No cover letter. No AI answers: we can tell, and we would rather hear from you.

Associate - Tech & Media (Commercial Disputes)
Department: Professional and Commercial Risk
Employment Type: Permanent
Location: Manchester

Description
Our Commercial Dispute Resolution team in Manchester is looking for an Associate (3–5 PQE) to support technology and media disputes and general commercial litigation.

Within our Professional and Commercial Risk group, the Manchester Commercial Dispute Resolution team works for a variety of large corporate and public sector clients with particular focus on IT, media and technology disputes. We act for suppliers and customers as well as insured and non-insured clients, including technology and media professionals.
Alongside technology and media work, the team handles general contractual disputes, defamation, IP litigation and wider commercial litigation (including urgent interim injunctions), supporting clients from across the firm when commercial disputes arise. We work closely with colleagues in Bristol and beyond, and run the firm's German desk, managing relationships with clients from Germany, Austria and Switzerland.

Your day-to-day work in our team will be as varied as dealing with urgent injunctive work, preparing advice notes to clients, handling claims from pre-issue through to trial, representing DAC Beachcroft at client and marketing events, assisting with team management and tacking part the firm's wider social and pro-bono activities.

Key Responsibilities
As part of the Commercial Dispute Resolution team you will:
• Run your own caseload of commercial disputes, with a focus on the IT, media and technology sectors;
• Handle matters from pre-action through to trial, including drafting pleadings, witness statements and advice;
• Work alongside senior colleagues on complex, high-value disputes;
• Help deliver our knowledge of key issues and provide meaningful advice to clients;
• Operate with autonomy, but with the benefit of support and supervision from leading practitioners at all times;
• Work in a highly collaborative environment, both within the team, across the firm, and with clients.

Skills, Knowledge and Expertise
• Around 3–5 years' PQE within a commercial litigation or commercial disputes practice;
• Experience of technology, media or IT matters, or a genuine interest in developing this specialism;
• Ability to take ownership and responsibility for matters;
• Good communication, relationship and client handling skills;
• Ability to deal confidently and professionally with clients on day-to-day issues;
• Ability to demonstrate a reasonable level of self-sufficiency, combined with an awareness of the boundaries of own competence/authority;
• Team oriented and collegiate with a willingness to share knowledge with and support other members of the team.

Additional Information
As a Disability Confident Scheme employer, we’re committed to providing an inclusive and accessible recruitment process. If you need any reasonable adjustments at any stage (including the application, assessment or interview process), please contact recruitment@dacbeachcroft.com in confidence with the vacancy reference in the subject line, and we’ll be happy to help.

Location: Daily Mail Headquarters, Derry Street, HSK, London, W8 5HY
Position: Full Time/Permanent

About the role

The Daily Mail is recruiting an Audience Editor to join our audience team, partnering with wider editorial teams to reach more readers and deepen engagement, on and off platform.

The right candidate will be able to analyse data to provide timely and actionable advice, and work with newsroom desks to ensure the best content is planned, commissioned, published and optimised, and that distribution is tailored to target audiences and platforms.&nbsp;

This is a fast-paced and dynamic role that requires a strategic thinking with excellent communication and analytical skills.

&nbsp;

&nbsp;Main Responsibilities

• Analyse real-time and historical audience and content performance data to identify trends and opportunities for growth and engagement on and off platform&nbsp;

• Translate data into actionable insights for the newsroom and provide desks with real-time advice on commissioning, optimisation and distribution

• Monitor search, social and audience trends to spot gaps in our coverage

• Help to identify repromotion opportunities and tailor stories for specific audiences, platforms and user journeys

• Execute experiments aimed at better attracting, engaging and retaining our target audiences

• Assist with planning for daily content and future news events

• Build strong relationships with editorial teams and work closely with them to implement audience engagement best practices

• Assist in developing content, distribution, growth and engagement strategies

• Stay up to date with industry trends and audience engagement best practices&nbsp;

&nbsp;

&nbsp;Person Specification

• Bachelor’s degree in journalism, data&nbsp;or a related field&nbsp;

• Experience in audience development, editorial data analysis or journalism, ideally within a subscriptions business

• Strong analytical skills, with experience using data to inform strategies and decisions

• Strong storytelling and communication skills, with the ability to collaborate effectively with multiple teams and stakeholders

• Good editorial judgement and the ability to work and make decisions quickly

• Knowledge of SEO and content optimisation best practices

• Familiarity with social media platforms and best practices for engagement

• Creative problem-solving skills and a willingness to experiment&nbsp;

&nbsp;

Package Description

Our benefits package increases the longer you’ve been with us. Here’s what to expect:

• 25 days’ holiday (increasing by 1 per year up to a total of 30)

• Pension plan and life cover

• Discounts on online shopping, dining cards and vouchers, and access to our Employee Assistance Programme

• Onsite gym, subsidised canteen and onsite nurse and GP clinics

Plus much more...

&nbsp;

Our Commitment

We are committed to increasing diversity and maintaining an inclusive workplace culture. We welcome applications from all qualified candidates regardless of their ethnicity, race, gender, religious beliefs, sexual orientation, age, marital status, or disability.

We are Disability Confident Committed. Please let us know if you require any recruitment documentation in other formats or if you require reasonable adjustments to be made during the recruitment process. Please be assured that any such information will be held separately to your recruitment application and will not be considered as part of the selection process.

