About the Company&nbsp;

In the coming decades, our world needs far more critical minerals including copper, lithium, and cobalt, to build electric infrastructure, vehicles, data centers, and electronics. The mining industry is making 10x fewer discoveries per dollar spent on exploration compared to 30 years ago because the easy-to-find, near surface deposits have largely been discovered. 

KoBold is the leading scientific mineral exploration, mine development, and technology development company. Our goal is to turn mineral exploration into a repeatable science to discover the minerals the world needs—by integrating artificial intelligence, human intelligence, and new technology. Our multidisciplinary teams of data scientists, engineers, and geologists work together to build data systems, design new sensors, and establish industry-leading workflows to develop and test subsurface predictions on our exploration projects.&nbsp;

&nbsp;

Our first discovery, Mingomba, is a high-grade copper deposit in Zambia, found after spending materially less than industry average. We are developing Mingomba with the same technical rigor that we apply to exploration. The Mingomba team brings together mine and processing engineers, geologists, data scientists, software engineers, and community, health &amp; safety, construction, and operations specialists. By combining industry knowledge and cutting edge technology, we are developing Mingomba into a world class project that has safer and more predictable outcomes for ourselves, partners, and communities. It is expected to create thousands of good jobs for generations.&nbsp;

&nbsp;

KoBold runs exploration programs in eight countries, all with the potential for another discovery.

&nbsp;

KoBold is privately held; investors include institutional asset managers T. Rowe Price and Canada Pension Plan Investments; technology venture capitalists Andreessen Horowitz, Breakthrough Energy Ventures, BOND Capital, Durable Capital, StepStone, and Standard Investments; and strategic natural resources companies BHP and Mitsubishi.

About the Role

This role will be responsible for creating technical and scientific content for internal and external audiences (such as investors, government officials, the public) about KoBold’s projects, science, and technology. You will collaborate closely with KoBold’s leaders, exploration teams, and technology teams to understand deeply and communicate compelling stories effectively in written, video, and graphical formats.

We are seeking an analytically minded producer, who has a track-record of overseeing the production of scientific or technical content for a variety of audiences. Our ideal candidate brings a scientific or technical background, a strong track record in content creation, and hands-on video editing and animation skills. However, we encourage individuals with strong analytical and technical skills, alongside storytelling and writing skills, to apply even if you do not have video production experience.&nbsp;

Note: please submit a portfolio with your application that includes examples of past graphic, video, and any other scientific storytelling work relevant to this role. Only applicants who submit a portfolio will be considered.

Responsibilities

• Act as an in-house scientific producer, managing the creation of content including video, written works, and graphics to visually tell stories to a variety of audiences

• Work closely with KoBold Metals’ leaders to identify high-priority story opportunities across KoBold

• Interview scientists and geologists across KoBold Metals to understand their areas of expertise, and produce coherent narrative arcs about the innovative work KoBold is undertaking&nbsp;

• Oversee video production tasks from pre-production through to post-production, including sourcing and managing vendors world-wide&nbsp;

• Initiate and/or create (with support from our graphic design team) technical figures and graphics

• Write, edit and provide feedback on written content, including reports, case studies, social media, and presentation scripts to tell scientific stories for investors and other external, and internal audiences

• Work with and advise internal staff on their scientific presentations, to ensure they are informative and accessible&nbsp;

• Travel to KoBold events and work sites to direct field shoots, scientific interactions and other activities to generate content about our field programs and operations

Qualifications

• Ability to understand technical information and turn it into compelling stories for non-expert audiences. A strong communicator who enjoys working with colleagues across the company.

• Strong writing and storytelling skills across a variety of formats, including social media

• A proficient executor with a keen eye for design details and editorial judgment to decide what to cut, emphasize, or reframe

• At least 5 years experience in a scientific or technical multimedia creation role for a public-facing brand or organization, or an equivalent combination of education and work experience.&nbsp;

• (Preferred) Proficiency in industry-standard graphic design, video editing and/or video production tools such as Premiere Pro, After Effects, Descript, Illustrator, and Figma.&nbsp;

• (Preferred) Experience in sourcing, hiring, and managing vendors for video; including filming, voiceover, and video editing/animation.

• Intellectual curiosity and eagerness to learn about all aspects of mineral exploration, particularly in the geology domain. Enjoys constantly learning such that you are driving insights through using our tools in exploration and willing to work directly with geologists in the field.

• Excitement about joining a fast-growing early-stage company, comfort with a dynamic work environment, and eagerness to take on an evolving range of responsibilities.

• Keen not just to execute projects, but to figure out how to best achieve the business objectives of the company.

• A valid passport and willingness to travel to observe our work at Mingomba (in Zambia) or at an exploration site around the world. Travel for this role typically does not exceed 5 trips per year.&nbsp;

&nbsp;

KoBold Metals is an equal opportunity workplace and an affirmative action employer. We are committed to equal employment opportunity for people of any race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, gender identity, sexual orientation, marital status, national origin, age, citizenship, disability, or veteran status.

&nbsp;

This position is Full-time.

&nbsp;

The US base salary range for this full-time exempt position is USD$100k - 150k, plus equity and benefits including 401k matching.

&nbsp;

Location: KoBold is a remote-first workplace. All candidates must be legally authorized to work in one of the following countries: United States, Canada, and UK.

Applicants must be authorized to work for any employer in the country in which the role is being hired. We are unable to sponsor or take over sponsorship of an employment visa at this time.

Mark43’s mission is to empower communities and their governments with new technologies that improve the safety and quality of life for all. We build powerful, scalable, and elegant software that sets a new standard for the tools upon which our first responders rely. Our users are diverse, and we are therefore committed to embracing diversity of thought and experience within our team.

We are seeking a Senior Integration Architect to design and deliver integrations for our UK customers. Mark43 works with a growing number of UK police forces, and this role is responsible for the integrations that connect Mark43 to their systems and to national policing and criminal justice services. You will manage UK interface projects from scoping through go-live and ongoing support, provide technical oversight of the partner and contractor teams who build integrations on our behalf, and ensure that their work meets Mark43’s standards. You will work closely with police forces, their suppliers and national system owners, as well as with Mark43’s UK delivery, engineering and customer success teams. This role reports to the Director of Integrations Architecture.

What You’ll Do

In this role, you will:

• Conduct scoping sessions with police forces to confirm which systems will connect to Mark43, how data will flow between them, and the effort required to deliver each integration.

• Prepare interface specifications and review them with forces and their suppliers through to formal sign-off before development begins.

• Review delivery partners’ integration designs, data mappings and test results, and approve their work before it is released to the customer.

• Coordinate onboarding, licensing and testing with the owners of national policing and criminal justice systems.

• Test integrations using force data within the UK, and work with forces to resolve mapping issues before user acceptance testing.

• Investigate integration issues in test and production environments using logs, monitoring tools and data queries, and work with engineering and support teams to resolve them.

• Work with force IT and network teams and Mark43’s cloud engineers to establish secure connectivity for integrations, both on-premise and in the cloud.

• Track the status of UK interface projects and report progress, risks and required actions to internal and customer stakeholders.

• Support contract and tender reviews by assessing integration requirements and confirming that they can be delivered.

&nbsp;

What You’ll Need

We are seeking a candidate with 8+ years of experience designing and delivering system integrations, preferably for UK policing, criminal justice or other public sector organisations. You should be able to manage multiple integration projects concurrently, work directly with customers and their suppliers, and oversee the work of partner and contractor teams. The role also requires strong technical skills, including the ability to interpret API specifications, build and validate data mappings, analyse logs, and query data to diagnose issues. This is not a software development role, but you should be comfortable using Kubernetes and CI/CD tools to deploy integrations, check their status and investigate failures.

This role involves access to police data that must remain in the UK. Candidates must have the right to work in the UK and be able to obtain and maintain Non-Police Personnel Vetting Level 3 (NPPV3). Candidates who already hold NPPV3 will be preferred.

The ideal candidate will also demonstrate the following qualities:

• Driven. You take the initiative to keep projects moving and resolve blockers without waiting for direction.

• Highly organised. You manage multiple concurrent projects and prioritise work effectively as deadlines and customer needs change.

• Accountable. You take ownership of project outcomes, including work delivered by partners and contractors.

• Composed under pressure. You respond to critical interface issues methodically and keep customers informed throughout.

• Strong communicator. You explain technical trade-offs clearly to both force project boards and engineering teams.

• Sound judgement. You make well-reasoned decisions when requirements are incomplete or still evolving.

Relevant Skills

Integration Design &amp; Delivery:

• REST and SOAP APIs; XML and JSON

• Data mapping, transformation and validation

• Message-based and file-based integrations, including secure file transfer

• Integration platforms (iPaaS)

Troubleshooting &amp; Diagnostics:

• Using logging and monitoring tools to investigate integration errors and failures

• Tracing messages end to end to identify where data is rejected, incorrectly mapped or lost

• Diagnosing connectivity, authentication and certificate issues

• SQL for querying and validating data

Cloud, Deployment &amp; Networking:

• Working knowledge of AWS and Linux

• Familiarity with containers and Kubernetes, including reviewing workload status and logs

• Familiarity with CI/CD and GitOps deployment tools such as Argo CD

• Networking fundamentals, including firewalls, private connectivity and certificates

UK Policing &amp; Criminal Justice (desirable):

• National systems such as PNC/LEDS, PND, IDENT1 and the Common Platform

• Command and control, custody, case management, intelligence and property systems used by UK forces

• Data protection requirements for police data, including UK GDPR and the Data Protection Act 2018

Delivery &amp; Stakeholder Management:

• Overseeing third-party and contractor delivery teams

• Reporting status and risk to customer project boards

• Reviewing contracts, statements of work and tender requirements for integration scope

&nbsp;

What We Offer&nbsp;

• 28 days&nbsp;holiday&nbsp;plus UK bank holidays&nbsp;

• Private medical, dental, and vision insurance&nbsp;through AXA Health and BUPA, fully paid for you and your dependents&nbsp;

• 18 weeks&nbsp;paid parental leave for primary caregivers plus a ramp-back programme&nbsp;

• Income protection&nbsp;(75% of salary) and&nbsp;death in service&nbsp;cover (4x salary), fully paid&nbsp;

• Pension&nbsp;through Nest with 3% employer contribution&nbsp;

• Gym reimbursement&nbsp;for you and your partner&nbsp;

• Equipment allowance&nbsp;to set up your home office&nbsp;

• AI tooling including Claude Code Enterprise and ChatGPT Enterprise licences provided&nbsp;

• Spring Health membership&nbsp;with therapy sessions and mental wellness tools, fully covered&nbsp;

• Company performance-based bonus&nbsp;

• Paid sabbatical&nbsp;of one month at your five-year anniversary&nbsp;

• Biannual hackathons, learning budget, and a team that genuinely invests in your growth&nbsp;

&nbsp;

What We Value&nbsp;

• Humility.&nbsp;You know the best ideas win, no matter where they come from. You ask questions before making&nbsp;assumptions&nbsp;and&nbsp;you're&nbsp;as happy being wrong as being right, because either way, the team&nbsp;gets to&nbsp;a better answer.&nbsp;

• Inclusivity.&nbsp;You respect&nbsp;expertise&nbsp;in all its forms and actively seek out perspectives different from your own. You make space for others and assume good intent.&nbsp;

• Excellence.&nbsp;You care about quality in your code, your reviews, and how you communicate.&nbsp;You're&nbsp;not satisfied with "it works" when it could be better, and you encourage the same standard in those around you.&nbsp;

• Diligence.&nbsp;You take ownership, mind the details, and understand that the software we build is used in moments that genuinely matter. You&nbsp;don't&nbsp;cut corners when people are depending on the outcome.&nbsp;

&nbsp;

Location

This role has travel to police forces and partner sites across the UK as required. As most of the Integrations Architecture team is based in the US, some meetings will take place in the UK afternoon or early evening.
Mark43 is approved to hire in Canada, the UK, and 36 U.S. states, including Alabama, Arizona, California (excluding San Francisco), Colorado, Connecticut, Washington D.C., Florida, Georgia, Iowa, Idaho, Illinois, Indiana, Kansas, Massachusetts, Maryland, Maine, Michigan, Minnesota, Missouri, North Carolina, Nebraska, New Hampshire, New Jersey, New Mexico, New York, Ohio, Oklahoma, Oregon, Pennsylvania, South Carolina, Tennessee, Texas, Utah, Virginia, Vermont, Washington, Wisconsin, and West Virginia. Before applying to a remote role, please ensure that you are able to perform the position in one of the states listed above. State locations and specifics are subject to change as our hiring requirements shift.&nbsp;

Our Privacy Notice describes how Mark43 uses and protects the personal information of prospective employees during the recruitment process. It informs you about our handling of the personal information you provide to us when you apply for a position in our organization and in general when you express your interest in joining our team.

As a part of Mark43's security measures all employees must: Engage in appropriate use of the company's electronic information resources; Become knowledgeable about and follow relevant security policies and guidelines; Protect the resources under their control, such as passwords, computers, and data that they create, receive, or download; and Promptly report security-related incidents and violations, and responding to official reports of security incidents involving their systems or accounts.

Mark43 is committed to the full inclusion of all qualified individuals. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex disability, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information. As part of this commitment, we will ensure that persons with disabilities are provided reasonable accommodations. If reasonable accommodation is needed, please email recruiting@Mark43.com requesting the accommodation.&nbsp;

As a Team Manager at Matalan&nbsp; you’ll be a key role model in our stores, showcasing our Matalan Values and behaviours whilst optimising sales and leading a high performing, energetic and adaptable team.

You’ll be coaching and motivating team members as an integral part of the store management team. As the store Team Manager you’ll also have responsibility for the running of the store in the absence of the store Manager and will use feedback from customers to create a great shopping experience.&nbsp;

If you’re looking for a successful career in Retail Management, a Team Manager role at Matalan could be a great start!

You’ll be...

• Driving sales targets and will explore sales opportunities

• A Role Model of outstanding Customer Service, Matalan Values and have a real passion for Retail

• Leading the implementation of seasonal layouts and visual guidelines throughout the store

• Opening and closing the store

• Up-skilling team members, giving regular feedback to drive performance

To be part of our team, we’d like you to....

• Have experience in a similar role in Fashion or Homeware Retail

• Be a confident communicator who understands how to engage and motivate others

• Be able to provide examples of leadership experience

• Have a good understanding of Visual Merchandising (VM)

• Have a proven ability to identify sales opportunities and drive new ideas

• Have good knowledge of operational processes and procedures within retail while remaining conscious of costs

• Be able to work under pressure and be adaptable to change

In addition to competitive salaries, we also offer the below core benefits:

• 20% colleague discount, which increases with length of service

• 25 days annual leave plus bank holidays (pro-rata basis dependant on contracted hours)

• Optional extra holiday buy scheme up to 5 days per year

• PLUS 1 extra free day leave to support your wellbeing

• Thrive Recognition Scheme&nbsp;

• Employee Assistance Programme &amp; Wellbeing support provided by the Retail Trust&nbsp;

• Life Assurance&nbsp;

• Retail Rewards platform offering discounts for multiple retailers&nbsp;

• Pension Scheme&nbsp;

• Access to a wide range of career development&nbsp;

• Additional benefits may apply depending on your role and area of the business

From humble beginnings to disruptive innovations in the retail industry, find out about how Matalan is ever-evolving here on our careers site.

We know as a team, we are stronger together – we champion equality for all and make lasting connections that go beyond work. We thrive off our inclusive culture, encouraging our colleagues to bring their true selves to work and contributing to collective creativity, open-mindedness and growth.&nbsp;

We want give every candidate the opportunity to perform at their best throughout the application and interview process and then ultimately in their role. If you require any adjustments during our recruitment process, please don’t hesitate to let us know. In the event that a high volume of suitable applications are received, the post may close prior to the specified closing date. Please apply as soon as possible if interested.&nbsp;&nbsp;

