London, hybrid, one day a week onsite
Up to £90,000 plus 10% cash allowance, 10% non contributory pension and discretionary bonus

We’re looking for a Senior Site Reliability Engineer with hands on Azure, Kubernetes and Terraform experience to join a major financial services organisation. Taking a "build it, own it, run it" approach, you’ll be accountable for service health and help improve how systems perform, scale and recover. 

As the team’s Senior Site Reliability Engineer, you’ll also represent SRE across the wider business, working with engineering and delivery colleagues to establish reliable ways of working.

The Role
• Keep systems healthy, reliable and ready to handle growing demand.

• Resolve incidents and keep colleagues and stakeholders informed.

• Improve monitoring, automate routine work and make releases safer.

• Work with engineering and delivery teams to tackle problems and manage risk.

• Guide colleagues and represent SRE across the wider business.

Requirements
• Hands on Azure, Kubernetes and Terraform experience.

• An Site Reliability Engineering (SRE) background with responsibility for running live services.

• Experience with microservices, containers and API management.

• Full stack monitoring and observability experience.

• Experience with DevOps, pipelines, releases and automation.

• Experience in a large organisation with established processes.

• Confidence working with stakeholders, leading improvements and supporting colleagues.

• Bicep, Azure DevOps, IT Service Management, ServiceNow and financial services experience would be useful.

Apply Now.

TAKE THIS PATH

&nbsp;

Our vision is to give everyone the belief they can make their move. We aim to make moving simpler,&nbsp;by giving everyone the best place to turn to and return to for access to the tools, expertise, trust, and belief to make it happen.

We’re home to the UK’s largest choice of properties and are the go-to destination for millions&nbsp;of people planning their next move, reading the latest industry news, or just browsing what’s on the market.&nbsp;

&nbsp;

Customer Invoicing Support Executive

Location: Milton Keynes (Hybrid working, 2 days per week in the office. Tues/Weds)

Reporting to: Customer Experience Team Leader

&nbsp;

As a Customer Invoicing Support Executive, you'll be part of a passionate team dedicated to delivering an outstanding experience for our partners. You'll provide efficient, timely support while building strong relationships and demonstrating the value we place on every partner interaction.&nbsp;

Engaging with partners every day, you'll use your excellent communication and problem-solving skills to understand their needs, resolve queries, and collaborate with teams across Rightmove to ensure a seamless and positive customer experience.&nbsp;

&nbsp;

What you’ll be doing&nbsp;

• Providing a seamless service to internal and external partners across multiple communication channels, within agreed standards&nbsp;

• Contributing to team objectives, projects and wider Rightmove initiatives&nbsp;

• Identifying process improvements and constructively contributing ideas&nbsp;

• Engaging with new technology and ways of working that improve the partner experience&nbsp;

• Taking ownership of your development, with support from the leadership team&nbsp;

&nbsp;

Who you are&nbsp;

• Passionate about doing the right thing, taking responsibility and exercising good judgement.&nbsp;

• Methodical and quality-focused, taking pride in delivering accurate work first time.&nbsp;

• Empathetic and customer-centric, always striving to exceed expectations.&nbsp;

• Driven by high standards, believing that "good enough is never good enough."&nbsp;

• Resilient and adaptable, comfortable managing increased workloads during peak periods.&nbsp;

• Self-motivated and able to work independently.&nbsp;

• Curious and eager to learn, embracing change and new responsibilities.&nbsp;

• Flexible and collaborative, willing to support wider teams when needed.&nbsp;

• Committed to understanding and contributing to the goals and success of the business.&nbsp;

• Is an excellent team player, loyal, reliable and punctual. &nbsp;

&nbsp;

What you’ll bring to the role&nbsp;&nbsp;

• A passion for delivering exceptional, customer-focused service.&nbsp;

• Strong knowledge of billing processes and the importance of accuracy.&nbsp;

• Excellent numeracy skills and a keen eye for detail.&nbsp;

• Clear communication skills and the ability to build strong relationships.&nbsp;

• Effective time management and prioritisation skills.&nbsp;

• The ability to remain calm and productive under pressure.&nbsp;

• Confidence using Excel, Word, and CRM systems.&nbsp;

• A proactive approach to problem-solving and taking ownership of queries.&nbsp;

&nbsp;

Life at Rightmove

Despite our growth, we’ve remained a friendly, supportive place to work, with employee #1 still working here!&nbsp; We’ve done this by placing the Rightmove Hows at the heart of everything we do. These are the essential values that reflect our culture, and include:

• We&nbsp;create&nbsp;value…by delivering results and building trust with partners and consumers.

• We&nbsp;think&nbsp;bigger…by acting with curiosity and setting bold aspirations.

• We&nbsp;care&nbsp;deeply…by being real, having fun, and valuing diversity.

• We&nbsp;move&nbsp;together…by being one team - internally collaborative, externally competitive.

• We&nbsp;make&nbsp;a difference…by focusing on delivering measurable impact.

&nbsp;

&nbsp;

We believe in careers that open doors and help our team develop by providing an open and inclusive work environment, offering ongoing&nbsp; &nbsp;training opportunities, and supporting charity fundraising events. And with 89% of Rightmovers saying we’re a great place to work, we’re clearly doing something right!&nbsp;

What we offer

• Cash plan for dental, optical and physio treatments.

• Private Medical Insurance, Pension and Life Insurance, Employee Assistance Plan.

• 27 days holiday plus two (paid) volunteering days a year to give back, and holiday buy schemes.

• Contributory stakeholder pension.

• Life assurance at 4x your basic salary to a spouse, family member or other nominated person in your life.

• Competitive compensation package.

• Paid leave for maternity, paternity, adoption &amp; fertility.

• Travel Loans, Bike to Work scheme, Rental Deposit Loan.

• Charitable contributions through Payroll Giving and donation matching.

• Access deals and discounts on things like travel, electronics, fashion, gym memberships, cinema discounts and more.

• We offer hybrid working with a minimum of 2 days in the office. For our roles, such as Field or Home-based positions, different working arrangements apply - full details will be shared during the recruitment process.

As an Equal Opportunity Employer, Rightmove will never discriminate based on age, disability, sex, race, religion or belief, gender reassignment, marriage / civil partnership, pregnancy/maternity or sexual orientation.&nbsp;

At Rightmove, we believe that a diverse and inclusive workforce leads to better innovation, productivity, and overall success. We are committed to creating a welcoming and inclusive environment for all employees, regardless of their background or identity, to develop and promote a diverse culture that reflects the communities we serve.

By applying, you confirm that you are aged at least 18 or over and&nbsp;that you’ve read and understood our Privacy Policy, which explains how we handle and protect your personal information during the recruitment process.

